                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Please write log messages for humans. You don't need to include every variable in the log _message_. Including variables in the log _entry_ means they're still captured in case you need them.\n\nSee https://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/anti-patterns.md#ill-defined-data-structuring-in-lg2-message-strings\n\nYou can write this as:\n\n```\nlg2::info(\"Found BridgeGpio config {LABEL}\", \"LABEL\", labelVal, \"NAME\", gpioName, \"POLARITY\", ..., \"TIME\", setupTime);\n```\n\nAlso why is the `\"TIME\"` entry not called `\"SETUP_TIME\"`? `\"TIME\"` is a bit general and ambiguous."
                },
